    airo:sourceDocId "3562" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b2686c2a0daa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hall says Gemini’s failings will at least help focus the AI safety debate on immediate concerns such as combating deepfakes rather than the existential threats that have been a prominent feature of discussion around the technology’s potential pitfalls." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b368127c7876> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Gemini makes a mess of generating historic images and pushes Google into culture war, Google promises fix" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b4cc477ec48a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Gemini Experiences Senior Director of Product Management Jack Krawczyk admitted to Fox News Digital in a statement on Wednesday that this was an issue his team was working on." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b4efd29c0fe6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google’s decision to pause image generation of people in Gemini comes less than 24 hours after the company apologized for the inaccuracies in some historical images its AI model generated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b743ab522653> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "‘We definitely messed up’: why did Google AI tool make offensive historical images?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bb34f9cda537> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the latest hiccup in the Alphabet-owned company's efforts to catch up with rivals OpenAI and Microsoft." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3577" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/be87db832d11> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google CEO Sundar Pichai says Gemini chatbot’s ‘woke’ AI disaster ‘completely unacceptable’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c1e7e78a4117> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3511] Google says it’s pausing the ability for its Gemini AI to generate images of people, after the tool was found to be generating inaccurate historical images." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c3b05228af76> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When OpenAI went through these issues in 2022, its technique for diversity insertion led to some awkward generations at first." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3515" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c517db2ec947> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google said Thursday that it was pausing its AI model’s ability to generate images of people after users pointed out that its Gemini AI was making historically inaccurate images of people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5fff2c5927e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Ben Thompson, the influential tech commentator behind the Stratechery newsletter, wrote Monday that Gemini’s responses appeared to have a consistent viewpoint that reflected a corporate culture in need of a shake-up." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c6471cd88cb0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Over time, OpenAI has refined its system prompts, now included with ChatGPT and DALL-E 3, to purposely include diversity in its outputs while mostly avoiding the situation Google is now facing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3515" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cd8dc1c6ff77> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Prabhakar Raghavan, the company’s senior vice president of knowledge and information, acknowledged the bug in a blog post published today." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cdd102629edf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's all likely to be an embarrassment and a hassle for Google in its competition with Microsoft and its partner OpenAI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3571" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cf06d1cfacfb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“I think it is just lousy software,” Gary Marcus, an emeritus professor of psychology and neural science at New York University and an AI entrepreneur, wrote on Wednesday on Substack." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d15d03996a6f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3572] Alphabet Inc.'s (GOOG) Google issued an apology for its AI chatbot Gemini, generating images of historical figures with inaccurate racial and ethnic depictions, attributing the errors to its attempt to create diverse results." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3572" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d9fc068bd0df> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The chatbot generated further outrage with its text responses after it refused to condemn pedophilia and claimed there was “no right or wrong answer” when asked if Adolf Hitler or Elon Musk is worse." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dac229416d98> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google found itself wrapped in another controversy Thursday afternoon when screenshots of a purported message to Gmail users suggested the widely used email service would be sunsetting." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/db5bcca6d42a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Red-faced Google apologizes after woke AI bot gives 'appalling' answers about pedophilia, Stalin" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc9acdac69e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to a report by Axios, Meta's Imagine AI image generator has also returned the similar kind of historical gaffes as Gemini." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3579" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd96cf798bee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After Google released its revamped Gemini in some parts of the world on February 8, some users earlier this week posted screenshots on social media showing how the chatbot was inaccurately depicting white-dominated scenes with racially diverse characters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/de641454bc39> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google apologized Friday for a tranche of historically inaccurate images generated on its Gemini AI image service." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e29f77724f66> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google’s ‘Woke’ Image Generator Shows the Limitations of AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e5f8a185f05f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google pauses Gemini's AI image generation features to fix historical inaccuracies" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3575" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e699eaf3d153> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Historically, AI models including OpenAI’s Dall-E have been plagued with bias." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e73d5514f0b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google is offering a mea culpa for its widely-panned artificial intelligence (AI) image generator that critics trashed for creating \"woke\" content, admitting it \"missed the mark.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3574" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ebd43f50565b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Since the launch of OpenAI's ChatGPT in November 2022, Google has been racing to produce AI software rivalling what the Microsoft-backed company had introduced." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3573" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ecea26a7bad3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3572] Alphabet Inc.'s (GOOG) Google issued an apology for its AI chatbot Gemini, generating images of historical figures with inaccurate racial and ethnic depictions, attributing the errors to its attempt to create diverse results." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3572" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/efdef85111e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3570] Google has paused the image generation feature of Gemini AI after receiving multiple complaints regarding its historical inaccuracies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f03bed933d06> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As part of the new service, Gemini offers an image generator, similar to Midjourney and OpenAI’s DALL-E." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f1adff8dd098> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Canny manipulation of the system – an approach known as “prompt injection” – can sometimes reveal them, however." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f507d3d7ace4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As noted by the New York Post, he posted screenshots of the exchange to X which revealed that the program could not outright condemn the behavior as a moral evil." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f523a74796d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google Apologizes For Inaccurate Gemini Photos: Tried Avoiding ‘Traps’ Of AI Technology" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f6913a5ad805> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "System prompts are written instructions that tell AI models how to behave, using natural language phrases." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3515" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f69b103f1148> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has, therefore, announced that: \"We're already working to address recent issues with Gemini's image generation feature." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3571" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fb17a5735e01> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“The ridiculous images generated by Gemini aren’t an anomaly. They’re a self-portrait of Google’s bureaucratic corporate culture,” computer scientist and investor Paul Graham wrote in a post on X." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3561" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fc76e5f503e3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NYPD has been using Clearview AI's facial recognition technology since 2018." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3560" .

