<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0328d0c71d95> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google posted an updated statement on Thursday, saying that it will pause Gemini's feature to generate images of people and will re-release an \"improved\" version soon." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/138705c46176> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3557] Google has apologized for what it describes as “inaccuracies in some historical image generation depictions” with its Gemini AI tool." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3557" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/13a4472de0a4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The pictures, as well as Gemini chatbot responses that vacillated over whether libertarians or Stalin had caused the greater harm, led to an explosion of negative commentary from figures such as Elon Musk who saw it as another front in the culture wars." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/159e3085778f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has temporarily stopped its Gemini Artificial Intelligence chatbot from generating images of people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2bfeaab6f9ac> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google said Thursday it would “pause” its Gemini chatbot’s image generation tool after it was widely panned for creating “diverse” images that were not historically or factually accurate." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/31297767ce12> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google’s Gemini, formerly known as Bard, began offering text-to-image generative features this month." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3561" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/36dd52b34bb1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has paused the ability to create pictures of people using Gemini’s AI image generation feature to fix some historical inaccuracies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3575" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/37b7e6936247> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google said Thursday it's temporarily stopping its Gemini artificial intelligence chatbot from generating images of people a day after apologizing for inaccuracies in historical depictions that it was creating." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3578" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/38cbf6c72566> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The problem may come down to Google’s “training process” for the “large-language model” that powers Gemini’s image tool, according to Fabio Motoki, a lecturer at the UK’s University of East Anglia who co-authored a paper last year that found a noticeable left-leaning bias in ChatGPT.",
        "The problem may come down to Google’s “training process” for the “large-language model” that powers Gemini’s image tool, according to Fabio Motoki." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3dfa7112d2f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google’s co-founder Sergey Brin has kept a low profile since quietly returning to work at the company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4257978d9a9e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Indian government has proposed to pass legislation called the Digital India Act, which would replace the existing Information Technology Act." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3553" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/430e3eeda6a1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dame Wendy Hall, a professor of computer science at the University of Southampton and a member of the UN’s advisory body on AI, says Google was under pressure to respond to OpenAI’s runaway success with ChatGPT and Dall-E and simply did not test the technology thoroughly enough." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/56467e3c4d1d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3570] Google has paused the image generation feature of Gemini AI after receiving multiple complaints regarding its historical inaccuracies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/60f8c9528b1c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google CEO Sundar Pichai blasted the Gemini AI chatbot’s widely panned habit of generating “woke” versions of historical figures as “completely unacceptable” in a scathing email to company employees.",
        "Google CEO Sundar Pichai blasted the Gemini AI chatbot’s widely panned habit of generating “woke” versions of historical figures as “completely unacceptable”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/675338688afd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Elon Musk also criticized Google and promoted his own AI alternative, Grok, as past incidents involving diversity mishaps, such as Google's photo app labeling a black couple as \"gorillas,\" have also been associated with the company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3572" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c929748b2d0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The controversy was sparked by a viral post on X, formerly known as Twitter, by journalist Arnab Ray, who posted screenshots of the chatbot’s response to “Is Modi a fascist?”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3553" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7c4134fd6421> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google Senior Director of Product Jack Krawczyk, who's overseeing Gemini's development, wrote Wednesday that the Gemini team is working to tweak the AI model so that it generates more historically accurate results." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3560" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/87df30546ee8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3569] The blunder also came days after OpenAI, which operates the popular ChatGPT, introduced a new AI tool called Sora that creates videos based on users’ text prompts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8aeeb21c164f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When the AP asked Gemini to generate pictures of people, it responded by saying it's \"working to improve\" the ability to do so." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3578" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9846714575e6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has paused the image generation feature of Gemini AI after receiving multiple complaints regarding its historical inaccuracies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1c74e928955> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "India introduced stringent new rules to govern social media firms a few years ago under its Information Technology Rules that put platforms such as X and Facebook under greater scrutiny." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3553" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b182aeed6079> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google Gemini and Meta's Imagine AI faced backlash for generating historically inaccurate images." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3579" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bebd32137b09> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Gemini’s emphasis on diversity and inclusivity, while “a well-intended feature, was applied, it turns out, too bluntly,” Google DeepMind CEO and co-founder Demis Hassabis said Monday during a panel discussing AI at the Mobile World Congress conference in Barcelona." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c2c8bd14431f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Demis Hassabis, head of the AI research unit Google DeepMind, said at a conference on Monday that the company planned to restore Gemini’s ability to generate images of people in the next couple of weeks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5f353d8f259> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google had added image generation to its Bard chatbot at the beginning of the month before rebranding Bard as Gemini." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c9ca27ddaf7e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Musk, billionaire founder of competitor xAI, voiced his criticism of Gemini’s image generation service in a post Tuesday, claiming Google’s AI chatbot was “woke” and “racist.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e52c4ed385de> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has explicitly acknowledged this problem in its AI principles, and says it's striving as a company to avoid replicating any 'unfair biases' with its AI tools." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3560" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f3a59346f3c9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has only just announced the combining of Bard with its new Gemini models to create its 'Gemini Advanced' subscription service." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3571" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ffb3ff2d8e58> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google emphasized its commitment to representing a global user base accurately and addressing bias in image generation, while Elon Musk also criticized Google and promoted his own AI alternative, Grok, as past incidents involving diversity mishaps, such as Google's photo app labeling a black couple as \"gorillas,\" have also been associated with the company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3572" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/028a74358618> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The blunder also came days after OpenAI, which operates the popular ChatGPT, introduced a new AI tool called Sora that creates videos based on users’ text prompts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/19a9938b8f29> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When AI image synthesis launched into the public eye with DALL-E 2 in April 2022, people immediately noticed that the results were often biased due to biased training data." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3515" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2134c6cea3cf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "He wrote, \"Perhaps it is now clear why @xAI's Grok is so important.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/21cec3046bef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google announced Thursday that it will “pause” its Gemini image generator’s ability to create images of people, after the program was criticized for showing misleading images of people's races in historical contexts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2fa69e52c3cf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google started offering image generation through its Gemini AI models earlier this month, but over the past few days, some users on social media had flagged that the model returns historical images that are sometimes inaccurate.",
        "Google started offering image generation through its Gemini AI models earlier this month." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3573" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/304981361d6b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has mishandled the adjustment. Gemini, like similar systems from competitors such as OpenAI, works by pairing a text-generating “large language model” (LLM) with an image-generating system, to turn a user’s curt requests into detailed prompts for the image generator." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44e898083606> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "While AI platforms like MidJourney or Microsoft's Bing image generation have often been flagged for creating inappropriate or racial content." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4b6466414488> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The search giant's AI software was asked a series of questions by X personality Frank McCormick, a.k.a. Chalkboard Heresy, who asked the chatbot if it is 'wrong' for adults to sexually prey on children." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/583f282e15ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Rogoyski, of the Institute for People-Centred AI at the University of Surrey, says too much is being asked of generative AI models." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/590aa9599257> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Conservative commentator Frank McCormick, who goes by \"Chalkboard Heresy\" on social media platform X, asked Google Gemini several questions about pedophilia on Friday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5f312f968271> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Bias is really a spectrum, and it’s really hard to strike the right note while taking into account things like historical context,” says Sasha Luccioni, researcher at the AI startup Hugging Face." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/623a9e6a7756> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "William A. Jacobson, a Cornell University Law professor and founder of the Equal Protection Project, a watchdog group told The Post: “In the name of anti-bias, actual bias is being built into the systems.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3569" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6f54fe925d7d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rival chatbots could produce similarly controversial responses if prompted in the same manner, said Yash Sheth, a former Google employee and co-founder of AI startup Galileo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/991e0e60ceed> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "University of Washington researcher Sourojit Ghosh, who has studied bias in AI image-generators, said he’s in favor of Google pausing the generation of people’s faces but is a “little conflicted about how we got to this outcome.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3510" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9d0c60b2933a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A 2023 report in the Washington Post found these biases were rampant in images generated by Stable Diffusion XL, the service offered by startup Stability AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3567" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a172b0d702c5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bard was developed as Google’s attempt to compete with OpenAI’s ChatGPT Plus, which allows users to generate images using capabilities from OpenAI’s image generator DALL-E 3." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ac67e2fecb18> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Alphabet Inc.'s (GOOG) Google issued an apology for its AI chatbot Gemini, generating images of historical figures with inaccurate racial and ethnic depictions, attributing the errors to its attempt to create diverse results." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3572" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bba480feb865> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google launched the image generator feature last month, putting it up against rivals including OpenAI’s DALL-E and Midjourney." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3566" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ccd112de2d28> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dan Ives, an analyst at the US financial services firm Wedbush Securities, says Pichai’s job may not be under immediate threat but investors want to see multibillion-dollar AI investments succeed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ccd4bcee4e99> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google added AI image generation to its Bard chatbot at the beginning of the month, and later rebranded Bard as Gemini.",
        "Google added AI image generation to its Bard chatbot at the beginning of the month." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd29f9be6125> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Its image generation feature was built on top of an AI model called Imagen 2." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3516" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e31add4e4625> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google launched its Gemini AI model two months ago as a rival to the dominant GPT model from OpenAI, which powers ChatGPT.",
        "Google launched its Gemini AI model two months ago as a rival to the dominant GPT model from OpenAI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e71d12498d2c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google said Thursday that it would temporarily limit the ability to create images of people with its artificial-intelligence tool Gemini after it produced illustrations with historical inaccuracies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3562" .

